lines=[keep.rstrip(),'','## 3. Celebration root cause and restoration','','Compared the original v1 source and actual v1/v3 frame sequences from their untouched backups. **The jump was not literally absent in shipped v3** at 412×915: it was replaced by a less legible choreography. V1 launched directly upward for **1.5s**, with **100ms** stagger and dedicated jump/swim poses. V2/v3 changed it to **0.9s**, spending its first **400ms moving DOWN to the board dock**, then only ~500ms airborne, with **350ms** stagger. The current starter map also reused the standing cutout for all poses. This made the action read as a shuffle rather than the original concurrent leap; before frames show it. No solver/completion-trigger failure or hidden-flyer bug was found.','', 'Restored v1-style direct upward arcs and concurrent launches: **1500ms flight / 100ms stagger**, with an 85px lift adapted to the current cutouts (v1: 65px). All current starter PNGs remain untouched and swappable in characters.js. A CSS lower-edge water fade helps the same cutouts read as soaking after landing. Retained timed splash rings, steam, per-landing sound/haptics, reaction, saved oranges and golden lily. Lantern/badge and lily/capy overlaps found in screenshot review were separated. Reduced motion still crossfades directly to soaking. First landing 1500ms; last landing 1900/2000/2100ms for 5/6/7 capys; reaction ≥2800ms.','', 'Before: `before-v3-flight-*.png`; original reference: `reference-v1-flight-*.png`; after: `after-v31-flight-*.png` plus all three `after-launch-{jun,bloom,remy}-{airborne,soaked}.png`. Frame labels are nominal sampling times, not a high-speed-camera claim.','', '## 4. End screen and original sizing — Mode A history','', 'Removed the small-height `height:auto / overflow:visible` fallback and 260px minimum lower area **for solved screens**. Baseline v3 normal solve produced a 784px document in a 780px viewport (the sampled buttons themselves happened to fit); the layout is now one safe-area-aware viewport. All three controls are fully visible with document height exactly viewport height after normal, boss 10, boss 30 and daily solves at **412×915 and 360×780**. Eight E2E cases cover the button rectangles and scroll. Daily’s Next pond opens the next uncleared campaign pond; after 30 it returns to Pond Path.','', '**Historical Mode A; latest Mode B default and measured table are above.** Board cap formula is `n×52 + (n−1)×3 + 6 + 16`: 52px cells, 3px gaps, 3px grid padding, 8px outer padding. Width is constrained by 4px side margins. Cells are **52px at every campaign size at 412px**. At 360px, seven 48px cells plus required spacing cannot fit; they remain **44.56px minimum**, above 44px. All cells are measured, not just inferred. 5px zone outlines remain. Spare height is shared around the play area and the flex lower section, never by growing the compact message card.','', '|Viewport|Grid|Board before → after px|Cell before → after px|','|--|--|--:|--:|']
for x in sizing:lines.append(f"|{x['viewport']}|{x['n']}×{x['n']}|{x['before_board_px']:.0f} → {x['after_board_px']:.0f}|{x['before_cell_px']:.2f} → {x['after_cell_px']:.2f}|")
lines+=['', 'Screenshot QA additionally caught the existing 360px seven-slot row clipping Relax. Narrow screens now use 24px counter **icons** (the switch remains ≥44px), and hide the optional daily date suffix so the header controls/oranges fit. New E2E rectangle checks cover both widths. This was the earlier smaller-cell choice, now superseded by Mode B above; color/pattern/art remain unchanged.','', '## 5. Haptics — moderately stronger','', '|Type|Old ms|New ms|','|--|--|--|','|Drag mark / clear tick|8|12|','|Legal capy|24|32|','|Illegal capy|[35,55,35]|[45,60,45]|','|Solve|[35,55,55,55,85]|[45,60,70,60,105]|','|Each water landing|12|18|','', 'Drag throttle stays **70ms**, movement threshold **10 CSS px**, single/double-tap window **280ms**. Only newly changed cells tick; already-marked/visited cells do not. The one persisted Haptics toggle suppresses every pattern. Missing/throwing APIs fail silently. Mocked tests verify exact patterns, new-cell/clear ticks, fast-drag throttling, mute and landing timing. Physical feel still needs S24 testing.','', '## 6. $0 original CC0 acoustic music','', 'Live source pages were opened and saved; all explicitly list **CC0**, with direct downloads requiring neither account nor payment. CC0 permits commercial/in-app copying, modification and distribution without fees. Evidence: `music-source-pages/`; full titles/authors/source and license URLs, date checked (**2026-11-09 EST**), credits and hashes: `assets/music/LICENSES.md`, `music-v3.1.json`. No Timberborn recordings/assets are used. The mood selection is based on source descriptions/instrumentation, not a claim of human listening or proven melodic provenance.','', '|Track / author|Source|Opus bytes|MP3 bytes|','|--|--|--:|--:|']
