lines+=['', f"All three are **CC0 1.0 Universal**: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/ . Combined audio **{music['total_audio_bytes']:,} bytes (4.99 MB / 4.76 MiB)**; audio + license **{summary['music']['audio_and_license_bytes']:,} bytes**, within the 5 MB aim. Stereo Opus 40kbps nominal + MP3 64kbps; −21 LUFS / −3dBTP normalization, 0.8s leading / 1.5s trailing fades. FFmpeg fully decoded all six, and browser metadata decoding passed for all six. Both formats are precached, not lazily downloaded.", '', 'WebKit’s source confirms Ogg/Opus arrived on iOS **18.4**: https://webkit.org/blog/16574/webkit-features-in-safari-18-4/ . `canPlayType` selects MP3 on older Safari; an Opus decoder error retries MP3 once. The service worker supports offline single-byte-range responses for iPhone media requests; tested 206 / 32-byte slice alongside all normal 200s.','', 'Settings has an independent, persisted **Music** toggle, default on but strictly silent until a trusted first touch/key on each page load. No media is allocated/played before interaction; autoplay rejection is caught. Existing v1/v2/v3 progress gets the new-field default without changing schema or losing progress/streak/powers. Effects off is not a music mute: the controls are deliberately separate. Music-off and explicit mute are respected; HTML media’s mute flag is not overridden. Gain **0.14** normal / **0.085** Relax (calmer, not muted); 800ms fade-in, 240ms toggle fade-out, immediate pause on hidden tab. Tracks rotate and wrap. In-app **Music credits** includes all authors, including Alex McCulloch’s requested name even though CC0 does not impose attribution. No external playback requests.','', '## 7. Verification, tests and visual review','', 'Campaign/daily data are byte-identical to shipped v3: **30 + 365 safe + 365 rock-eligible = 760** unique, connected boards, all no-guess. Python full-permutation oracle and separate JS row DFS/proof checks were re-run. **5,840** actual transformed daily outputs across both eligibility states also pass determinism/uniqueness/pure logic. Deduction set remains house-single + shared-conflict, no branching. Updated `verification-v3.1.json/.md`; `verify-v3.1.log`, `daily-v3.1.log`. All per-level solution counts/rocks/techniques remain recorded.','', '```sh','npm run test:unit','CAPYDOKU_REPORT_VERSION=v3.1 CAPYDOKU_SCREENSHOT_DIR=reports/screenshots-v3.1/regression npm run test:e2e','python3 scripts/verify-v3.py','TZ=America/New_York node scripts/verify-daily-v3.mjs','python3 scripts/contact-sheet-v3.1.py','```','', f"**66/66 unit + 69/69 e2e PASS**, no failures/skips/flaky tests and **0 browser console/page errors**. Final e2e began **{start}**, duration **{stats['duration']/1000:.2f}s**. All **42/42 precache URLs return 200 online AND offline**, including music. Actual shipped-v3 → v3.1 SW upgrade, old-cache removal, progress/streak preservation, unseen-query offline reload and Range audio pass; inherited v1/v2 migrations/upgrades still pass. Logs `unit-v3.1.log`, `e2e-v3.1.log`; JSON `playwright-v3.1.json`, `TEST-SUMMARY-v3.1.json`; HTML `playwright-html-v3.1/`.",'', f"Screenshot audit: **{shots['count']} native PNGs** = **{shots['native_412x915']} at exactly 412×915**, plus **{shots['additional_native_360x780']} explicitly labeled 360×780** additions. Location `screenshots-v3.1/`, smaller captures `360x780/`, inherited coverage `regression/`. Main `contact-sheet-v3.1.png`; paged `contact-review-v3.1-*.png` and `contact-regression-review-v3.1-*.png`. All pages and key full-size captures were visually inspected; clipped Relax at 360 and celebration overlaps were fixed before final run.",'', '## 8. Local release boundary, backups and honest limits','', f"The completed batch’s cache bump is **prepared locally only: `{pre['cache']}`** (was `capydoku-v3-5288463b8ae5`). This uses the explicit conditional permission for a finished batch; **no live link was updated**. Further accidental cache rebuilds remain guarded. Initial held-v3 audit is retained in `cache-hold-v3.1-initial.json`; current local candidate in `cache-hold-v3.1.json`. Screenshot review/approval is still needed before any future publish. No v3.1 archive was requested/generated; optional packaging now targets a separate v3.1 filename and cannot overwrite the frozen v3 tar.",'', f"Snapshot audit: v1 **74/74**, v2 **226/226**, v3 **345/345**, pre-extension v3.1 **{backup['snapshots'][3]['original_files_checked']}/{backup['snapshots'][3]['original_files_checked']}** original hashes match. All **36/36 shipped v3 tar files** match `app-v3-backup/`; tar hash is unchanged. Extra rollback point `app-v31-ui-backup/`. Details `backup-integrity-v3.1.json`; runtime change hashes `runtime-diff-v3-v3.1.json`.",'', '**v6 completed handoff arrived during this round, but has no explicit v6 approval marker/status; not integrated.** notes.md/manifest were checked. Its proposed Hint return, Relax defensive-power disable, final-cell Peek restriction and generic/v1 celebration pieces conflict with the existing user brief; none were acted on. Inventory/status in `v6-status-v3.1.json`. No mockup or backup was modified by this implementation.','', 'Real iPhone/Safari/WebKit, S24 hardware, physical haptic strength, hardware mute/interruptions/notches, and human judgment of musical mood/quality remain **unverified**. Chromium includes actual local audio playback/decoding plus mocks, not physical listening. Existing localStorage eviction and finite daily-bank limitations remain in `KNOWN-ISSUES.md`.']
